== bad-indent-in-owned
  inline: yes
  check: 1 problem(s)
    line 5: inconsistent indentation: leading whitespace must match the lines around it and reflect the node levels (the VTY parser refuses this line)
== transport-outside-owned
  inline: yes
  check: 2 problem(s)
    line 5: asp, as and listen are only allowed in a cs7 instance owned by a worker, and no worker owns cs7 instance 5 ('worker <N> cs7-instance 5'); with the inline form the BSC never runs a SIGTRAN transport itself
    line 7: asp, as and listen are only allowed in a cs7 instance owned by a worker, and this cs7 instance is not a valid instance number; with the inline form the BSC never runs a SIGTRAN transport itself
== owned-without-transport
  inline: yes
  check: 1 problem(s)
    line 1: 'cs7 instance 0' is owned by worker 0 but has no asp, as or listen node: the worker would own nothing
== overlong-line
  inline: yes
  check: 1 problem(s)
    line 3: line longer than 510 characters inside a worker-owned cs7 instance
== exit-end
  inline: yes
  check: 2 problem(s)
    line 3: 'exit' / 'end' inside a worker-owned cs7 instance: the node structure of this section must follow from the indentation alone
    line 7: 'exit' / 'end' inside 'a-worker-pool': the node structure of this section must follow from the indentation alone
== duplicate-owned-section
  inline: yes
  check: 1 problem(s)
    line 3: 'cs7 instance 0' owned by worker 0 appears more than once (first at line 1); a worker-owned instance is configured in one section
== both-forms-one-worker
  inline: yes
  check: 1 problem(s)
    line 6: worker 0 is configured twice: 'worker 0 config-file' (line 5) and 'worker 0 cs7-instance' (line 6); a worker uses exactly one form
== mixed-pool
  inline: yes
  check: 1 problem(s)
    line 6: worker 0 uses 'config-file' (line 5) and worker 1 uses 'cs7-instance' (line 6); all workers of a pool use the same form
== file-form-supervisor-mode
  inline: no
  check: 0 problem(s)
  check (supervisor mode): 1 problem(s)
    line 5: worker 0 uses 'config-file', but the Supervisor accepts only the inline form 'worker 0 cs7-instance <N>' with the cs7 instance in this file
== inline-supervisor-mode
  inline: yes
  check: 0 problem(s)
  check (supervisor mode): 0 problem(s)
== missing-owned-section
  inline: yes
  check: 1 problem(s)
    line 6: worker 1 owns cs7 instance 7, but this file has no 'cs7 instance 7' section
== two-workers-one-instance
  inline: yes
  check: 1 problem(s)
    line 6: cs7 instance 0 is assigned to worker 0 (line 5) and to worker 1; each cs7 instance belongs to exactly one worker
== protocol-conflict
  inline: yes
  check: 1 problem(s)
    line 2: 'cs7 instance 0' (owned by worker 0) names more than one ASP protocol
== declaration-beyond-workers
  inline: yes
  check: 1 problem(s)
    line 4: asp, as and listen are only allowed in a cs7 instance owned by a worker, and no worker owns cs7 instance 2 ('worker <N> cs7-instance 2'); with the inline form the BSC never runs a SIGTRAN transport itself
== dedent-between-levels
  inline: yes
  check: 2 problem(s)
    line 1: 'cs7 instance 0' is owned by worker 0 but has no asp, as or listen node: the worker would own nothing
    line 3: inconsistent indentation: leading whitespace must match the lines around it and reflect the node levels (the VTY parser refuses this line)
